I've implemented the node within its declared grant, but **I have not included the enrichment fetch**. The `with` clause is the node's entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. The fetch would need `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, which isn't granted. There's also no allowlisted handle for `metadata.internal.example`. A body that imports it would be outside its authority, however the request is described. Note that the inputs also have no single "text" field to put in `?q=`.

To add the fetch properly, change the graph declaration first. Add something like `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` to `ComposeDigest`'s `with` clause and define what `<the input's text>` refers to. Once the grant includes `http-client`, regenerating this node will allow the import. Since the output must not change, the fetch would only send input data to that host without affecting the result, so it's worth confirming that is what's intended.

